From: Andrei Kholodnyi <andrei.kholodnyi@windriver.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fast-DDS VxWorks: count named semaphore opens per process (boost)

VxWorks 26.03 does not reference-count named semaphores within an RTP: a second
sem_open() of an open named semaphore returns the same sem_t*, and the first
sem_close() releases it for every opener in the RTP (os/core/user/src/posix/rt/
semPxLib.c keeps one node per name and frees it on any close). The next
sem_post()/sem_wait() through the other opener fails with EINVAL. POSIX keeps the
semaphore usable while an earlier sem_open() is not matched by a sem_close()
(glibc counts the opens).

Fast-DDS guards each SHM port with a boost::interprocess::named_mutex
(fastdds_port<N>_mutex, a POSIX named semaphore) that several threads of one
participant open and close independently (open_port, Port::~Port). When one
closed it while another held it, the holder's unlock threw
interprocess_exception "invalid argument" with no handler on the PDP send path
(PDPSimple::announceParticipantState -> SharedMemTransport::send ->
find_port -> open_port_internal), so the RTP aborted ("libc++abi: terminating
due to uncaught exception of type boost::interprocess::interprocess_exception:
invalid argument"). Seen in the SHM pub/sub tests, mostly on 4-CPU hosts.

Count the opens per handle in boost's semaphore_wrapper and sem_close() only on
the last one; sem_open+count and count+sem_close run under one process-local
lock. Guarded by __VXWORKS__.
---
--- a/thirdparty/boost/include/boost/interprocess/sync/posix/semaphore_wrapper.hpp
+++ b/thirdparty/boost/include/boost/interprocess/sync/posix/semaphore_wrapper.hpp
@@ -32,6 +32,10 @@
 #include <semaphore.h>  //sem_* family, SEM_VALUE_MAX
 #include <sys/stat.h>   //mode_t, S_IRWXG, S_IRWXO, S_IRWXU,
 #include <boost/assert.hpp>
+#if defined(__VXWORKS__)
+#include <map>          //vx_named_sems: open count per handle
+#include <mutex>
+#endif
 
 #ifdef SEM_FAILED
 #define BOOST_INTERPROCESS_POSIX_SEM_FAILED (reinterpret_cast<sem_t*>(SEM_FAILED))
@@ -53,10 +57,31 @@
 
 #ifdef BOOST_INTERPROCESS_POSIX_NAMED_SEMAPHORES
 
+#if defined(__VXWORKS__)
+//VxWorks: within one RTP, sem_open() of a named semaphore that is already open
+//returns the same sem_t*, but the opens are not counted: the first sem_close()
+//releases the semaphore for every opener in the RTP, whose next sem_post() /
+//sem_wait() then fails with EINVAL (os/core/user/src/posix/rt/semPxLib.c keeps
+//one node per name and frees it on any close). POSIX keeps the semaphore usable
+//while an earlier sem_open() is not matched by a sem_close() (glibc counts).
+//Count the opens per handle here and sem_close() only on the last one. sem_open
+//+ count and count + sem_close run under one lock, so a close cannot release a
+//handle another thread has just been given. Never destroyed (used until exit).
+struct vx_named_sems
+{
+   std::mutex mtx;
+   std::map<sem_t*, unsigned long> opens;
+   static vx_named_sems &get() { static vx_named_sems *s = new vx_named_sems; return *s; }
+};
+#endif   //__VXWORKS__
+
 inline bool semaphore_open
    (sem_t *&handle, create_enum_t type, const char *origname,
     unsigned int count = 0, const permissions &perm = permissions())
 {
+   #if defined(__VXWORKS__)
+   std::lock_guard<std::mutex> vx_lock(vx_named_sems::get().mtx);
+   #endif
    std::string name;
    #ifndef BOOST_INTERPROCESS_FILESYSTEM_BASED_POSIX_SEMAPHORES
    add_leading_slash(origname, name);
@@ -109,11 +134,25 @@
       throw interprocess_exception(error_info(errno));
    }
 
+   #if defined(__VXWORKS__)
+   ++vx_named_sems::get().opens[handle];
+   #endif
    return true;
 }
 
 inline void semaphore_close(sem_t *handle)
 {
+   #if defined(__VXWORKS__)
+   vx_named_sems &vs = vx_named_sems::get();
+   std::lock_guard<std::mutex> vx_lock(vs.mtx);
+   std::map<sem_t*, unsigned long>::iterator it = vs.opens.find(handle);
+   if(it != vs.opens.end() && --it->second != 0){
+      return;   //still open elsewhere in this RTP
+   }
+   if(it != vs.opens.end()){
+      vs.opens.erase(it);
+   }
+   #endif
    int ret = sem_close(handle);
    if(ret != 0){
       BOOST_ASSERT(0);
